  "conclusion": "LongMemEval-S's dates support day resolution and no finer. At day resolution question_date is inert: no session is dated after its question in 500/500 cases, proximity and recency orderings are identical at every granularity, and under exponential decay the origin cancels from every pairwise ratio (max relative deviation 4.51e-13). At minute resolution 76 questions have a session logged after the question -- never by a full day, which is why day truncation hides it -- and 43 have gold evidence in one, 21 of them entirely. Treating the question timestamp as a retrieval cutoff, which is what a deployed memory system must do, therefore scores zero on those 21 by construction."
